course: dictionary
lesson: 9651
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you need the words around them to know which one is meant. «The subject of the story was a brave little mouse.» Here subject means the topic: what the story is about.
explain: «The Mock Turtle's school subjects are puns too.» The words school subjects tell you that subjects here are school lessons, like maths, English or science.
explain: In grammar, the subject is the person or thing that does the action of a verb. In «The dog barks», the dog is the subject, and the verb barks goes with it. Ask yourself: who or what is doing the action?
explain: Subject can also mean likely to be affected by something. «Prices are subject to change» means the prices might be altered. Swap your meaning into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Subject can mean a school lesson, such as maths or science.
fact: Subject can mean the topic of a talk, a story or a painting.
fact: In grammar, the subject is the person or thing doing the action of the verb.
fact: «Subject to change» means it might be altered, so check the context before you pick a meaning.
fact: In «Each of the boys has a bike», the subject is «each», so the verb is «has».
exercise: «The subject of the story was a brave little mouse.» What does subject mean here? | A school lesson | *What the story is about | The verb in the sentence | A person ruled by a king or queen
exercise: In «The dog barks», which part is the subject? | *the dog | barks | loudly | barks loudly
exercise: «Reeling and Writhing» are the Mock Turtle's jokes for which school subjects? | *Reading and writing | Maths and science | History and geography | Music and art
test: «The shop's prices are subject to change.» What does subject to change mean? | It is a school lesson | *It might be altered | It is a king's rule | It will never change
test: In «Each of the boys has a bike», which word is the subject? | *each | boys | bike | has
exam: In an email, the line «Subject: Trip to the zoo» tells you what? | *What the message is about | The lesson at school | A person ruled by a king | The verb in the message
